        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Arctotis acaulis is a species of flowering plant in the family Asteraceae and is an endemic species found in the Cape Provinces, South Africa."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Etymology\nThe species name acaulis means without a stem, from Greek a which means without, and caulis meaning stem of a plant.{{source needed|reason='Caulis' is not Greek but Latin.|date=March 2025}} The name refers to the species growth habit."
          }
        ]
